WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:26.860
I summon Gear Golem the Moving Fortress in defense position.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.530
Another monster to defend with?

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:34.310
Yugi, you shouldn't be having this duel!

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:37.200
You can't have a fair duel against a Ghoul!

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.220
You're wrong, Jonouchi.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:44.050
I'll fight fair and square to the end and defeat him.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:49.500
A true duelist never leaves the battlefield, no matter who the opponent is.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:51.360
Yugi...

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:54.760
I won't let you summon Exodia!

00:01:54.760 --> 00:02:00.770
Comeback  Chain Destruction

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:11.420
Yugi is incredible.

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:14.880
He figured out the Rare Hunter's strategy in only a few turns.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:23.550
Yugi, you've taught me again about a duelist's confidence and pride.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.120
Kid, congrats on figuring out my strategy.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:38.270
But the next card I'll draw is Left Arm of the Forbidden One, the fifth card I need.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:43.270
Exodia will be completed on my next turn!

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:47.720
What can you possibly do in one turn?

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:57.680
Brother, I can't approve of this duel!

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:59.220
Just wait, Mokuba.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:04.700
As the commissioner of this tournament, I can't let him get away with cheating!

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:08.700
I know how terrifying Exodia is more than anyone else.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.280
Exodia?

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:11.900
That's even more reason!

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.220
I thought you wanted to defeat Yugi!

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:16.870
What if Yugi loses here?

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.510
That's fine with me.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.080
If he loses, he isn't much of a duelist.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:27.870
But as my only rival, he won't lose.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:29.720
My turn!

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:31.850
I set a card.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:35.490
Chimera the Flying Mythical Beast attacks!

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.590
Chimera Impact Dash!

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:41.800
I end my turn.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.930
You ended your turn!

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:50.610
What's wrong?  All you can do is destroy my defending monsters?

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:55.750
I see my victory.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.960
When I draw this card, you're finished.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:03.760
Damn!  Even though Yugi figured out his strategy, he's still in trouble!

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.020
Do something, Yugi!

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.030
My turn.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:10.820
I draw my card-

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:11.430
Now!

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:13.400
I activate my trap card!

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:14.640
What?

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:15.920
Time Seal!

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:19.120
This skips your Draw Phase.

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.900
A desperate trap.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:26.820
But I get a Draw Phase every turn.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:32.580
I'm still going to win when I draw my next card.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:35.690
He managed to survive this turn.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:39.400
Jonouchi's Red-Eyes in on the line in this duel.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.690
And Battle City...

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:46.560
...is my fight to regain my lost memories.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:50.820
I can't afford to lose.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:54.310
This one card will determine my destiny.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:58.850
I believe in our deck that we built together!

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:01.580
My card, guide me!

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.480
Lightforce Sword!

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:18.800
It banishes a card from your hand for three turns.

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:22.450
This will seal away your Exodia!

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:23.830
What?

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:29.240
But if it doesn't strike an Exodia card in his hand, I lose.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.280
Go, Lightforce Sword!

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:35.450
What?

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.550
Exodia's right arm!

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:45.160
He did it!  Yugi sealed away one of the parts!

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:53.000
I tribute Chimera to summon Summoned Skull!

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:01.000
Attack Gear Golem!

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.400
Magic Lightning!

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:13.010
Nice!  He's turning the tables!

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:14.420
Take him down, Yugi!

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:20.370
Even if you draw the final Exodia part next turn, Exodia won't be completed!

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:22.790
My turn.

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:24.600
I draw a card.

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:27.930
What's wrong?

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:30.430
Didn't you draw the card you wanted?

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:32.540
You should be happy.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:42.480
What's with him?

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:44.250
Did the shock drive him insane?

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:49.420
I expected you to figure out my strategy from the start!

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:50.680
What?

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:55.280
You didn't think I'd have a plan to stop your Exodia-sealing strategy?

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:58.100
Take this!

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.660
Swords of Revealing Light!

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:02.180
What?

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:05.970
Swords of Revealing Light?

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:12.400
Your monsters can't attack for three turns.

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:18.650
Your Lightforce Sword's effect will end before my Swords of Revealing Light's effect does.

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:21.150
Exodia will be completed!

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:25.320
I'm still going to win!

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:33.050
Damn!  I thought Yugi would turn the tables!

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:37.670
Brother, Yugi is really going to lose!

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:41.600
No, the real battle will now begin.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:46.920
If you're my true rival, then win the duel, Yugi!

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:49.680
My turn.

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:52.800
I draw a card and end my turn.

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:56.640
What happened to your fighting spirit?

00:07:56.640 --> 00:08:04.060
You must do something before Lightforce Sword's effect ends, but will you think of a plan in time?

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:09.220
My deck has three copies of each Exodia part.

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:14.420
So if I draw one of the two Right Arms in my deck...

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:19.420
...I'll win without having to wait for Lightforce Sword's effect to end.

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:22.760
What's so funny?

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:26.460
It's true that Swords of Revealing Light is a problematic card.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:29.030
But it's not invincible.

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:31.100
It's too late to say that.

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:36.920
Either I beat Swords of Revealing Light or you draw the remaining Exodia part.

00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:42.700
Either way, this duel will end within three turns!

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:44.700
My turn.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:46.170
I draw a card!

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:49.460
I already have this Exodia card.

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:51.700
It's fine.

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:56.210
As long as he can't attack, I don't have to be nervous.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:59.150
Yugi...

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:01.620
Don't worry, Jonouchi.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.820
I promise to get your Red-Eyes back.

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:06.520
My turn!

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:08.450
I set a card!

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:12.890
And I summon Alpha The Magnet Warrior!

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:14.840
In attack position!

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:21.220
You summoned a monster instead of giving up.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:23.050
How pointless.

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:24.600
Are you sure?

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:29.060
I'll tell you the Exodia deck's biggest weakness.

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:29.780
What?

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:39.120
Exodia is special because you need to gather five specific cards in your hand.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:43.200
The more parts you have, the more cards remain in your hand.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:46.100
So you have fewer cards to place on your field.

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:56.140
The Exodia deck's biggest weakness is that you don't have enough monsters on your field!

00:09:57.220 --> 00:10:00.510
Look.  Your field is empty.

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:05.780
But my monsters' combined attack points is almost 4000.

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:09.720
When we start battling again, you're finished in an instant!

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:11.660
You're bluffing!

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:14.180
Are you sure about that?

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:19.070
You'll feel their power soon enough.

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:39.150
Yugi...

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:42.920
Jonouchi, just watch.

00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:47.590
Whoever trusts their own deck will win this duel.

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:49.250
My turn!

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:51.560
I got another double.

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:55.860
It's true that I don't have any monsters on my field.

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:59.500
But Swords of Revealing Light's effect is still active.

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:01.950
What's wrong?

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:07.600
Even if he's bluffing, I have to be careful.

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:12.820
If I summon my extra copy of Exodia in defense position...

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:16.990
...even if he manages to destroy Swords of Revealing Light next turn...

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:20.290
...I can block one of his attacks.

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:23.290
There's no drawback to this plan!

00:11:26.710 --> 00:11:29.820
Exodia the Forbidden One in defense position!

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:37.450
Your deck is made of counterfeit cards.

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:40.170
That's why you couldn't trust it to the end.

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:43.840
I was waiting for this moment!

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:45.920
I flip over my trap card!

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:48.280
Chain Destruction!

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:54.890
What is this?

00:11:55.240 --> 00:12:01.280
When you summon a monster, this card destroys its copies in your hand and deck!

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:02.760
What?

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:05.970
Vanish!

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:16.800
Exodia comes to life when you gather all the cards in your hand.

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:25.100
Since one part is gone from your hand and deck, you can never complete Exodia.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:28.150
No way...

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:32.270
My Exodia...

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:39.700
Since you're using counterfeit cards, you can never control Exodia!

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:41.970
I activate my trap card!

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:46.800
Dust Tornado!

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:49.680
It destroys Swords of Revealing Light!

00:12:55.660 --> 00:12:57.060
My turn!

00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:58.490
Monster Reborn!

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:01.180
Chimera resurrects!

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:06.780
Chimera, attack the last card on his field!

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:08.370
Impact Dash!

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:16.360
You no longer have any monsters to defend with.

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:20.330
Go, Summoned Skull and Alpha The Magnet Warrior!

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:22.010
Attack him directly!

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:27.920
By attacking together, they gain 200 attack points!

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.320
Thunder Magnet Sword!

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:44.330
You did it, Yugi!

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:52.800
He did it!  Yugi won!

00:13:53.550 --> 00:13:57.360
Yugi won the first duel of the tournament, as expected.

00:13:57.800 --> 00:13:59.680
I can't sit back and relax.

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:03.370
I'm going to Battle City!

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:08.750
As Battle City commissioner, I'm going to patrol the city.

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:14.600
If you find the God Cards, tell my brother immediately!

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:21.460
You did it, Yugi.

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:22.340
Yeah.

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:33.150
Under the rules, I'm taking Jonouchi's Red-Eyes and your Puzzle Card.

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:41.590
These counterfeit cards...

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:49.850
I lost...

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:54.270
My strongest deck lost...

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:05.400
Help me.  He's coming...

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:08.790
Yugi, he's acting weird.

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:14.520
The Millennium Item's symbol!

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:17.780
Marik is coming...

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:27.000
It's been a while, Yugi.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:29.950
The strongest duelist who defeated Pegasus.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:36.120
You're currently talking to the weakest of the Rare Hunters.

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:39.660
My Ghouls are actually not this weak.

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:42.820
Hey, what's he talking about?

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:46.060
Oops.  Sorry to surprise you.

00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:49.260
You're not currently talking to this man.

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:54.640
I'm in a different location from where you are.

00:15:55.040 --> 00:16:02.030
I implanted my memories inside him, so I can control him whenever I want.

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:04.630
Just like this.

00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:11.410
He's spooky!

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:13.080
Who are you?

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:17.630
I've been chosen by a Millennium Item, just like you.

00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:22.340
All this power comes from my Millennium Rod.

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:24.680
Millennium Rod?

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:31.900
An enemy with a new Millennium Item will appear before you soon.

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:38.070
This show was how I say hello.

00:16:39.500 --> 00:16:41.540
My name is Marik.

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:43.500
Marik!

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:47.880
Marik, what are you Ghouls after?

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:51.600
To collect the God Cards.

00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:54.820
The three rare cards that have revived in modern times.

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:56.490
God Cards?

00:16:56.720 --> 00:17:02.500
In ancient Egypt, there were three stone tablets that contained dark powers.

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:08.870
Obelisk the Tormentor, Slifer the Sky Dragon and The Winged Dragon of Ra.

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:18.310
The one who collects all the God Cards will gain the title of the Pharaoh and the power to conquer the world.

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:21.250
Power to conquer the world?

00:17:22.170 --> 00:17:26.420
We Ghouls already have two God Cards.

00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:32.550
And someone in this city has the remaining card.

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:36.020
Yugi, the game has only begun.

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:40.980
There's a Rare Hunter with a God Card somewhere in this city.

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:48.020
If you meet him, even with your skills, you'll be defeated instantly.

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:50.740
That won't happen.

00:17:50.740 --> 00:17:56.200
I won't let you have the title of the Pharaoh or the power to conquer the world!

00:17:56.540 --> 00:18:02.740
Even if a Rare Hunter with a God Card appears before me, I won't lose!

00:18:04.670 --> 00:18:06.730
How promising.

00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:11.660
I'll regain my memories by winning these battles.

00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:16.470
Marik, your Millennium Rod has called me to this battle!

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:19.240
I promise to defeat you.

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:22.780
Fine, chosen one.

00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:25.910
It's the start of the millennium battle!

00:18:26.970 --> 00:18:29.210
I'm looking forward to it.

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:34.470
He fainted.

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:36.970
He has the power to control others.

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:40.100
Where is Marik hiding?

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:44.600
Jonouchi, this is your card.

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:51.420
Yugi, I can't take that Red-Eyes right now.

00:18:54.840 --> 00:19:03.150
If I accept that card so easily, I feel like I'll be further away from becoming a true duelist.

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:05.080
True duelist...

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:11.880
Yugi, you're the closest to what I believe is a true duelist.

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:20.840
I felt that I was approaching your level when I dueled you at Duelist Kingdom.

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:25.170
But I was being arrogant.

00:19:25.750 --> 00:19:26.970
Jonouchi...

00:19:27.280 --> 00:19:32.780
You won fair and square against a cheater without compromising your principles.

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:36.410
I learned a lot from you again.

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:39.820
You have a duelist's pride that I don't have.

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:44.380
For me, Red-Eyes is an irreplaceable card.

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:47.720
My partner and I have fought together until now.

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:50.300
That's why I can't take it.

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:54.240
Red-Eyes won't approve of how I am.

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:59.300
So Yugi, take care of that card for now.

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:04.540
I've prepared a 40-card deck for today's tournament.

00:20:04.860 --> 00:20:09.180
I have a Puzzle Card and the right to participate in the tournament.

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:12.780
You gave me this Time Wizard.

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:15.620
This is my final rare card.

00:20:17.510 --> 00:20:21.220
I want to become a true duelist.

00:20:21.580 --> 00:20:25.160
No, not "want."  I "will" become a true duelist during Battle City.

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:34.550
Yugi, when I keep winning and become a true duelist, I want you to duel me again.

00:20:36.370 --> 00:20:37.570
Okay.

00:20:38.020 --> 00:20:40.480
Let's duel when that time comes, Jonouchi.

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:42.780
Thank you, Yugi.

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:48.750
Jonouchi, I'll wait for you.

00:20:48.960 --> 00:20:52.480
I'll hold on to your Red-Eyes until then.

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:59.520
There they are!  I finally found them!

00:20:59.520 --> 00:21:01.210
Yugi!  Jonouchi!

00:21:01.580 --> 00:21:03.040
All right!

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:05.180
The tournament has only started!

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:07.140
Who wants to take me on?

00:21:12.260 --> 00:21:14.060
Just wait, Red-Eyes.

00:21:14.060 --> 00:21:16.640
I promise to get stronger.

00:21:17.050 --> 00:21:19.290
Yugi, that's when...

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:21.220
We'll meet again.

00:21:21.220 --> 00:21:23.080
Hey, Yugi!

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:25.940
Yugi?  Jonouchi?

00:21:28.360 --> 00:21:30.430
Wait up!

00:21:45.040 --> 00:21:50.280
Jonouchi's first opponent is Esper Roba, the duelist who defeated Dinosaur Ryuzaki.

00:21:50.400 --> 00:21:54.000
He uses psychic powers to predict his opponent's strategy.

00:21:54.160 --> 00:22:00.450
Jonouchi said that he'll face opponents stronger than himself to become a true duelist.

00:22:00.450 --> 00:22:02.320
Will he really be okay?

00:22:02.320 --> 00:22:04.650
If you lose, you're finished!

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:08.590
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Esper Roba
Danger of the Psychic Deck

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:10.080
Duel, standby!

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:28.560
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:29.360 --> 00:22:33.930
I feel like I've been here

00:22:34.470 --> 00:22:43.610
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:43.910 --> 00:22:55.120
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:57.990 --> 00:23:02.630
Time passes bit by bit

00:23:03.300 --> 00:23:07.900
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:08.470 --> 00:23:13.010
Will never change

00:23:13.670 --> 00:23:18.280
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:18.910 --> 00:23:23.480
To be who I am

00:23:24.080 --> 00:23:28.720
I've kept searching for something

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:33.430
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:36.360
I learned that's the answer

00:23:37.160 --> 00:23:43.470
From now until forever...
